('33126','15','','10316','MySQL: Calculated value of innodb_log_file_size','mysql.innodb_log_file_size','1m','7d','365d','0','0','','','','',NULL,NULL,'(last(//mysql.innodb_os_log_written) - last(//mysql.innodb_os_log_written,#1:now-1h)) / {$MYSQL.INNODB_LOG_FILES}','','0','','','','','0',NULL,'`Innodb_log_file_size` is calculated as: (`innodb_os_log_written`-`innodb_os_log_written`(time shift -1h))/`{$MYSQL.INNODB_LOG_FILES}`. `Innodb_log_file_size` is the size in bytes of the each InnoDB redo log file in the log group. The combined size can be no more than 512 GB. Larger values mean less disk I/O due to less flushing checkpoint activity, but also slower recovery from a crash.','0','30d','0','',NULL,'3s','','','','200','1','0','','','0','0','0','0','0','0','0','e5413d85449e4baea683c6365808cc17','MYSQL: CALCULATED VALUE OF INNODB_LOG_FILE_SIZE'),
