('42535','7','','10351','Windows: Memory pool non-paged',E'perf_counter_en["\\Memory\\Pool Nonpaged Bytes"]','1m','7d','365d','0','3','','B','','',NULL,NULL,'','','0','','','','','0',NULL,'This measures the size, in bytes, of the non-paged pool. This is an area of system memory for objects
that cannot be written to disk but instead must remain in physical memory as long as they are allocated.
There is a possible memory leak if the value is greater than 175MB (or 100MB with the /3GB switch).
A typical Event ID 2019 is recorded in the system event log.','0','30d','0','',NULL,'3s','','','','200','1','0','','','0','0','0','0','0','0','0','3af0a0717da747849c2b5a2ebfa61a2c','WINDOWS: MEMORY POOL NON-PAGED'),
('42536','7','','10351','Windows: Memory pages per second',E'perf_counter_en["\\Memory\\Pages/sec"]','1m','7d','365d','0','0','','','','',NULL,NULL,'','','0','','','','','0',NULL,'This measures the rate at which pages are read from or written to disk to resolve hard page faults.
